Fetch a URL as compact Markdown (default), text, or HTML (max {{ .MaxFetchSizeKB }}KB output; 5MB input); no AI processing. HTML-to-Markdown conversion removes scripts, styles, and hidden markup while preserving headings, lists, tables, code, and links. Prefer Markdown for readable pages to reduce tokens; choose HTML explicitly when markup is needed. For analysis or extraction use agentic_fetch.
{{- if .GhAvailable }} For GitHub content when an exact repo, issue, or PR link is provided, use `gh` CLI in bash instead.{{- end }}

Normal mode is anonymous and remains the default. Request `mode: user` only when the user asks or browser authentication is needed. User mode always requires explicit user consent for this request or the current session, even with automatic tool approval enabled. The user selects a browser profile on the execution host; fetch copies matching cookies into memory and uses that browser's default family/version user agent. Redirects use matching cookies from the same selected profile. Cookies are never written back to the browser, and cookie values are redacted from returned text and diagnostics. This is an HTTP fetch, not browser automation: JavaScript, browser extensions, custom user-agent overrides, and browser-only challenges are not reproduced. Denied or unavailable user mode does not silently fall back to anonymous access.
